  "id": "DrugBank_DB05578 - MONDO_18055",
  "verbalization": "Ramucirumab, a monoclonal antibody, is implicated in the treatment of hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC) through its indication for liver cancer and its relationship with sorafenib, a tyrosine kinase inhibitor. The evidence suggests that Ramucirumab may serve as a potential therapeutic option for pediatric hepatocellular carcinoma, as it is linked to sorafenib, which is itself indicated for this condition. The pathways highlight a chain of indications where Ramucirumab, through its interaction with sorafenib, may influence the progression or management of pediatric HCC. The shared indication for sorafenib across multiple paths reinforces the possibility of a mechanistic link between Ramucirumab and the disease, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be elucidated. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Ramucirumab could be repurposed for pediatric HCC, particularly in cases where sorafenib is already being used.",
